/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_GeneratorsPeriodic Periodic tables
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Generators
 * @brief Inspect phase conventions for sine, saw, square and triangle waves.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsPeriodic_Goal Goal
 * Make waveform reference points explicit so a caller can align oscillators,
 * modulation sources and lookup tables predictably.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsPeriodic_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Generators_Periodic_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsPeriodic_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * Sine[0]=0%; expected=0%
 * Sine[1]=100%; expected=100%
 * Sine[2]=0%; expected=0%
 * Sine[3]=-100%; expected=-100%
 * Saw phase 0 starts at zero; half-cycle=-1
 * Square phase 0=+1; half-cycle=-1
 * Triangle quarter-cycle=+1; three-quarter-cycle=-1
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * These points establish the phase origin and polarity conventions, not merely
 * the nominal waveform shape.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsPeriodic_Code Implementation
 * \include Generators/Periodic/Shared.cpp
 */
